4 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186514914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515494 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515006 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515494 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515494 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515494 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515494 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515494 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186514914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515494 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c8d9ffbc-23ef-519d-9512-884d3bb1903d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515570 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515570 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108881" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515570 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515570 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y+1}{2}=\\frac{z}{4},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩=25.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515570 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "83aacc67-1785-59c3-94ae-6f65bea01fe4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515570 #edb/ref 1074 "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(-2,-1,0)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,2,4⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-2,-1,0⟩+t⟨3,2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2+3t,-1+2t,4t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,-1+2t,4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ & =25 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,-1+2t,4t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ & =25 \\\\ 3(-2+3t)-(-1+2t)+2(4t) & =25 \\\\ -6+9t+1-2t+8t & =25 \\\\ 15t & =30 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(2),-1+2(2),4(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,3,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(4,3,8).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
